abstract: >-
  A unified, machine-checked Lean 4.35.0 (Mathlib v4.35.0) and exact-arithmetic
  research repository consolidating three Pauli contextuality tracks: (1) spectral
  bounds, floor-saturating states including the infinite pure-CCZ determinant family
  |Psi_{3m}>, exact four-qubit C3 binary completion optima (368 vs 344), N=4..5
  double-counting ladders, and Jonah's Conjecture E across all nine vertex cases
  for all N >= 4; (2) exact contextuality degrees (7^k - 5^k)/2 and (6^k - 4^k)/2
  for k disjoint copies of the Peres-Mermin square and Mermin pentagram (answering
  Section 6 of Muller and Saniga, arXiv:2609.19862v1); and (3) exact finite-tree
  sequential contextuality evidence bounds and a constructive setting-bias attack
  on the Peres-Mermin square. Not externally peer reviewed; AI-assisted under human
  direction.
